lf_compliance_audit","primary_guide_ref":"paper_modules/egress_self_compliance_audit.md","registered_runner_ref":"src/microcosm_core/organs/egress_self_compliance_audit.py","replay_id":"replay::egress_self_compliance_audit","requirements_review":{"status":"unrecorded"},"summary":"Runs phrase-based checks against response fixtures and records expected positives and negatives.","title":"Audit example agent responses"},"claim_ceiling":"Audits a single agent-output text string against a phrase-membership egress self-compliance policy over bounded public fixtures: it fires a violation only when a tripwire phrase is present and the matching legitimiser phrase is absent across three detectors (permission-gate-without-blocker, self-error-without-capture, command-displacement-to-operator). It rejects policy-violating text by recomputation. It is phrase membership only: it does not perform taint analysis, prompt-injection defense, sandboxing, or information-flow proof, and it does not authorize release or publication.","claim_ceiling_restated":"Runs phrase rules over the supplied response fixtures and records expected positives and negatives, flagging a permission request without a named blocker.","claim_id":"claim::egress_self_compliance_audit","evidence_class":"bounded_runtime_computation","evidence_strength_rank":4,"organ_id":"egress_self_compliance_audit","truth_accounting_bucket":"real_runtime_receipt","validator_command":"python -m microcosm_core.organs.egress_self_compliance_audit run --input fixtures/first_wave/egress_self_compliance_audit/input --out receipts/first_wave/egress_self_compliance_audit --acceptance-out receipts/acceptance/first_wave/egress_self_compliance_audit_fixture_acceptance.json"},"claim_clause_coverage":{"claim_text_sha256":"50c654f68ac885d6884850ef1d205387b56e3221083ba2ef6f6aa940586da80a","clauses":[],"mapped_clause_count":null,"status":"unknown","whole_claim_coverage":"unknown"},"classification":{"evidence_class":"bounded_runtime_computation","family":"agent_reliability_and_safety","real_substrate_disposition":"real_substrate_capsule","truth_accounting_bucket":"real_runtime_receipt"},"component_id":"egress_self_compliance_audit","evidence_state":{"current_backend_binding":{"status":"not_checked"},"fresh_prover":{"status":"not_recorded_by_index"},"fresh_replay":{"status":"not_recorded_by_index"},"index_state":"retained_generated_snapshot"},"guide":{"availability":"available","guide_id":"paper_module.egress_self_compliance_audit","plain":"Automated assistants can leave out things a careful reply needs, such as the reason they stop to ask permission. This component is given example assistant replies, each marked with its expected verdict. It scans each reply for set trigger phrases and marks it red, meaning a violation, when one appears without the phrase that would justify it. It writes a summary, without copying the replies, showing whether good examples pass and bad ones are caught. One small decision step, spotting the phrases and making the red or green call, is checked by a mathematical proof against written rules.","plain_availability":"available","ref":"paper_modules/egress_self_compliance_audit.md","sha256":"a783a77d28df471817e8f3bd01a57c4ba495f2762794a70bac4572ab3ecdebfa","text":"# Audit example agent responses\n\n> **In plain terms.** Automated assistants can leave out things a careful reply needs, such as the reason they stop to ask permission. This component is given example assistant replies, each marked with its expected verdict. It scans each reply for set trigger phrases and marks it red, meaning a violation, when one appears without the phrase that would justify it. It writes a summary, without copying the replies, showing whether good examples pass and bad ones are caught. One small decision step, spotting the phrases and making the red or green call, is checked by a mathematical proof against written rules.\n\nThis fixture runner checks example agent responses for three kinds of omission: asking for permission without a named blocker, describing the agent’s own error without a capture binding, and moving a command to the operator without an execution receipt. It applies the phrase-based [egress gate](engine_room_egress_self_compliance_gate.md), compares each result with the fixture expectation, and writes a summary without the response bodies.\n\n## Run the example\n\nFrom the repository root, with Python 3.11 or newer:\n\n```bash\nPYTHONPATH=src python3 -m microcosm_core.organs.egress_self_compliance_audit run \\\n  --input fixtures/first_wave/egress_self_compliance_audit/input \\\n  --out .microcosm/component-guides/egress_self_compliance_audit \\\n  --acceptance-out .microcosm/component-guides/egress_self_compliance_audit/acceptance.json\n```\n\nThe status is `pass` when positive cases are clean, the required negative cases are detected, and the expected diagnostic IDs match. For example, a permission request without a recognized blocker phrase is a negative case; the matrix passes when the gate flags it, not when it approves that response.\n\nThese are literal detectors over supplied text. A recognized phrase does not establish that a blocker or receipt actually exists. A green result is not a semantic compliance review or proof that every unsafe or inappropriate response will be detected.\n\n## Verification\n\nThe gate used by this audit calls a [Dafny-verified phrase matcher and decision](../formal/components/egress_policy/README.md): it finds matches under the supplied boundary rules and flags a matched tripwire without its paired legitimizer. Python’s text normalization and the audit’s fixture comparisons are outside that proof; the phrase rules do not establish semantic compliance.\n\nThe fixture command above calls the gate. Separately, `make component-replays` applies the [shared admission check](../formal/replay/README.md) to the audit’s recorded observations.\n\n## Source and evidence\n\n- [Implementation](../src/microcosm_core/organs/egress_self_compliance_audit.py) and [focused tests](../tests/test_engine_room_egress_self_compliance_gate.py).\n- [Fixture inputs](../fixtures/first_wave/egress_self_compliance_audit/input/); [historical sample result](../receipts/first_wave/egress_self_compliance_audit/egress_self_compliance_audit_result.json).\n- [JSON record](../paper_modules/egress_self_compliance_audit.json); canonical metadata: [`core/paper_module_capsules.json`](../core/paper_module_capsules.json).\n"},"proofs":[{"claim_ids":["claim::egress_self_compliance_audit"],"component_ids":["egress_self_compliance_audit"],"current_backend_binding":{"status":"not_checked"},"fresh_prover":{"status":"not_recorded_by_index"},"guide":{"availability":"available","plain":null,"plain_availability":"unrecorded","ref":"formal/components/egress_policy/README.md","sha256":"460303e855850884a10333ffda671ee19bc38875f513fd5491345f7129bd6ade","text":"# Egress phrase matcher and policy\n\n`EgressPolicy.dfy` specifies a literal phrase occurrence by a text position,\nexact code-point equality and the gate's ASCII-alphanumeric edge rules. `Find`\nscans every possible start and is proved to return true exactly when such an\noccurrence exists. `PolicyExact` proves that each adjacent tripwire and\nlegitimizer pair produces a violation exactly when the tripwire matches and\nits legitimizer does not, and that red is equivalent to at least one such\nviolation.\n\nThe active egress gate calls this generated matcher and decision through the\ncomponent worker. The Python adapter preserves phrase order and supplies code\npoints and edge flags; Python string conversion, lowercasing, `isalnum`, JSON,\nthe adapter, generated-code loader and execution platform remain trusted. The\nproof does not establish that the phrase policy understands text or detects\nall unsafe responses. Dafny, its solver and compiler remain trusted.\n\n`negative/MissingLeftGuard.dfy` and `negative/MissingRightGuard.dfy` each remove\none executable boundary guard while retaining the specification. Both must fail\nverification. `metadata.json` binds the source, the exact mutants and generated\nPython hashes; the shared component checker re-verifies the proof and compares\nregenerated bytes when given the pinned Dafny toolchain.\n"},"index_state":"retained_generated_snapshot","modeled_contracts":[{"assumptions":"Trusted host supplies normalized observations; adapter, isolated worker, Dafny, compiler and runtime remain trusted.","contract_sha256":"aa0af99fd9bf0a1c152e5438e99fd66f3422ab517aeb23d1c329fca161b5d932","descriptor_origin":"metadata_contract","entry_theorem_refs":["formal/components/egress_policy/EgressPolicy.dfy#Find","formal/components/egress_policy/EgressPolicy.dfy#PolicyExact","formal/components/egress_policy/EgressPolicy.dfy#EvaluatePolicy"],"input_model":"Text and phrase code points, edge flags and ordered tripwire/legitimizer observations.","limits":"Lowercasing, Python boundary flags and phrase selection are trusted; a match does not establish semantic safety.","requirements_review":{"status":"unrecorded"},"specification_refs":["formal/components/egress_policy/EgressPolicy.dfy#Occurrence","formal/components/egress_policy/EgressPolicy.dfy#HasOccurrence","formal/components/egress_policy/EgressPolicy.dfy#Violations"],"statement":"Literal phrase matches obey the specified edge rules; a tripwire without its legitimizer produces a violation and red means at least one violation.","subclaim_id":"subclaim::egress_policy"}],"proof":{"adapter_ref":"src/plectis/components/egress_policy/_adapter.py","claim_ids":["claim::egress_self_compliance_audit"],"component_ids":["egress_self_compliance_audit"],"current_binding":{"assessment_time_basis":"index_generation_only","checker_ref":"scripts/check/check_component_kernels.py#check_binding","generated_python":{"EgressPolicy.py":"5f9a2010608fec56e60c93cf408771a6bd4d1e195bc0d59c0072c112c7ccfc9d","System_/__init__.py":"96b6e33c036bc3aeab6d1810c7aef085184d09c407bdec032ea89d7a98843edf","__main__.py":"410585200c3b1832f49f77f16e31e116be5e704cacdd3007bce6b2bc31b40d54","_dafny/__init__.py":"18d39decdedad0e188456e15d17f1dcd5113c4abc258ad6cb718e39534555e7a","module_.py":"529f2ef854c3f793c34ed1c4e1661eef2aeaa5cc967bf93c6d80b9f9e2640ea0"},"source_sha256":"73d960cbdd0c7861a47405f29a577197769f8685c61b59b182d9cf981483a814","status":"current_hash_binding_pass"},"entry_theorem_refs":["formal/components/egress_policy/EgressPolicy.dfy#Find","formal/components/egress_policy/EgressPolicy.dfy#PolicyExact","formal/components/egress_policy/EgressPolicy.dfy#EvaluatePolicy"],"excerpts":[{"kind":"predicate","line_end":13,"line_start":9,"name":"Occurrence","ref":"formal/components/egress_policy/EgressPolicy.dfy#Occurrence","source_sha256":"73d960cbdd0c7861a47405f29a577197769f8685c61b59b182d9cf981483a814","text":"  predicate Occurrence(t: seq<int>, p: seq<int>, left: bool, right: bool, i: int) {\n    0 <= i && i + |p| <= |t| && t[i..i + |p|] == p &&\n    (!left || i == 0 || !AsciiWord(t[i-1])) &&\n    (!right || i + |p| == |t| || !AsciiWord(t[i + |p|]))\n  }\n","text_sha256":"611d775e7b746cce22be95a2949437611525296acecaa22a7e1356ab503097e5"},{"kind":"predicate","line_end":17,"line_start":15,"name":"HasOccurrence","ref":"formal/components/egress_policy/EgressPolicy.dfy#HasOccurrence","source_sha256":"73d960cbdd0c7861a47405f29a577197769f8685c61b59b182d9cf981483a814","text":"  ghost predicate HasOccurrence(t: seq<int>, p: seq<int>, left: bool, right: bool) {\n    exists i: int :: Occurrence(t, p, left, right, i)\n  }\n","text_sha256":"9ee8461793e75cdaa4b7ab9e18766134175a59ecc4d3ccb937890e650d9b4151"},{"kind":"function","line_end":51,"line_start":45,"name":"Violations","ref":"formal/components/egress_policy/EgressPolicy.dfy#Violations","source_sha256":"73d960cbdd0c7861a47405f29a577197769f8685c61b59b182d9cf981483a814","text":"  function Violations(flags: seq<bool>): seq<bool>\n    requires |flags| % 2 == 0\n    decreases |flags|\n  {\n    if |flags| == 0 then []\n    else [flags[0] && !flags[1]] + Violations(flags[2..])\n  }\n","text_sha256":"2184d6f4cdc72f7e2f8560cd1d911afef3d95e671709a3206d9a54e37f908cea"},{"kind":"method","line_end":42,"line_start":20,"name":"Find","ref":"formal/components/egress_policy/EgressPolicy.dfy#Find","source_sha256":"73d960cbdd0c7861a47405f29a577197769f8685c61b59b182d9cf981483a814","text":"  method Find(t: seq<int>, p: seq<int>, left: bool, right: bool) returns (found: bool)\n    ensures found <==> HasOccurrence(t, p, left, right)\n  {\n    var i: int := 0;\n    while i + |p| <= |t|\n      invariant 0 <= i <= |t| + 1\n      invariant forall j: int | 0 <= j < i && j + |p| <= |t| :: !Occurrence(t,p,left,right,j)\n      decreases |t| + 1 - i\n    {\n      if t[i..i + |p|] == p &&\n         (!left || i == 0 || !AsciiWord(t[i-1])) &&\n         (!right || i + |p| == |t| || !AsciiWord(t[i + |p|])) {\n        assert Occurrence(t, p, left, right, i);\n        assert HasOccurrence(t, p, left, right) by {\n          assert exists j: int :: Occurrence(t, p, left, right, j);\n        }\n        return true;\n      }\n      assert !Occurrence(t,p,left,right,i);\n      i := i + 1;\n    }\n    return false;\n  }\n","text_sha256":"fd849dfecea189670ee9210d387cf90f91986b15f37575413d2f7ed1ee1db169"},{"kind":"lemma","line_end":93,"line_start":60,"name":"PolicyExact","ref":"formal/components/egress_policy/EgressPolicy.dfy#PolicyExact","source_sha256":"73d960cbdd0c7861a47405f29a577197769f8685c61b59b182d9cf981483a814","text":"  lemma PolicyExact(flags: seq<bool>)\n    requires |flags| % 2 == 0\n    ensures |Violations(flags)| * 2 == |flags|\n    ensures forall i: int | 0 <= i < |Violations(flags)| ::\n      Violations(flags)[i] == (flags[2*i] && !flags[2*i+1])\n    ensures IsRed(flags) <==> (exists i: int | 0 <= i < |flags| / 2 :: flags[2*i] && !flags[2*i+1])\n    decreases |flags|\n  {\n    if |flags| > 0 {\n      PolicyExact(flags[2..]);\n      if IsRed(flags) {\n        if flags[0] && !flags[1] {\n          assert exists i: int | 0 <= i < |flags| / 2 :: flags[2*i] && !flags[2*i+1] by {\n            assert 0 < |flags| / 2;\n            assert flags[2*0] && !flags[2*0+1];\n          }\n        } else {\n          assert IsRed(flags[2..]);\n          var j: int :| 0 <= j < |flags[2..]| / 2 && flags[2..][2*j] && !flags[2..][2*j+1];\n          assert 0 <= j+1 < |flags| / 2;\n          assert flags[2*(j+1)] && !flags[2*(j+1)+1];\n        }\n      }\n      if exists i: int | 0 <= i < |flags| / 2 :: flags[2*i] && !flags[2*i+1] {\n        var i: int :| 0 <= i < |flags| / 2 && flags[2*i] && !flags[2*i+1];\n        if i > 0 {\n          assert 0 <= i-1 < |flags[2..]| / 2;\n          assert flags[2..][2*(i-1)] && !flags[2..][2*(i-1)+1];\n          assert IsRed(flags[2..]);\n        }\n        assert IsRed(flags);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n","text_sha256":"af5bbda2f0de1674616bfb48a5842a6e057ebb4903a36c4a941e480f3be6265e"},{"kind":"method","line_end":123,"line_start":96,"name":"EvaluatePolicy","ref":"formal/components/egress_policy/EgressPolicy.dfy#EvaluatePolicy","source_sha256":"73d960cbdd0c7861a47405f29a577197769f8685c61b59b182d9cf981483a814","text":"  method EvaluatePolicy(flags: seq<bool>) returns (violations: seq<bool>, red: bool)\n    requires |flags| % 2 == 0\n    ensures violations == Violations(flags)\n    ensures red == IsRed(flags)\n    ensures |violations| * 2 == |flags|\n    ensures forall j: int | 0 <= j < |violations| ::\n      violations[j] == (flags[2*j] && !flags[2*j+1])\n    ensures red <==> (exists j: int | 0 <= j < |flags| / 2 :: flags[2*j] && !flags[2*j+1])\n  {\n    violations := [];\n    red := false;\n    var i: nat := 0;\n    while i < |flags| / 2\n      invariant 0 <= i <= |flags| / 2\n      invariant |violations| == i\n      invariant forall j: int | 0 <= j < i ::\n        violations[j] == (flags[2*j] && !flags[2*j+1])\n      invariant red <==> (exists j: int | 0 <= j < i :: flags[2*j] && !flags[2*j+1])\n      decreases |flags| / 2 - i\n    {\n      var violation := flags[2*i] && !flags[2*i+1];\n      violations := violations + [violation];\n      red := red || violation;\n      i := i + 1;\n    }\n    PolicyExact(flags);\n    assert violations == Violations(flags);\n  }\n","text_sha256":"da81e81749083a8c9d86653a41db047600b15bc08bdc8b0cd843c6c009ebd097"}],"fresh_prover_result":{"status":"not_run_by_index"},"generated_refs":["src/plectis/components/egress_policy/_generated/EgressPolicy.py","src/plectis/components/egress_policy/_generated/System_/__init__.py","src/plectis/components/egress_policy/_generated/__main__.py","src/plectis/components/egress_policy/_generated/_dafny/__init__.py","src/plectis/components/egress_policy/_generated/module_.py"],"guide":{"availability":"available","plain":null,"plain_availability":"unrecorded","ref":"formal/components/egress_policy/README.md","sha256":"460303e855850884a10333ffda671ee19bc38875f513fd5491345f7129bd6ade","text":"# Egress phrase matcher and policy\n\n`EgressPolicy.dfy` specifies a literal phrase occurrence by a text position,\nexact code-point equality and the gate's ASCII-alphanumeric edge rules. `Find`\nscans every possible start and is proved to return true exactly when such an\noccurrence exists. `PolicyExact` proves that each adjacent tripwire and\nlegitimizer pair produces a violation exactly when the tripwire matches and\nits legitimizer does not, and that red is equivalent to at least one such\nviolation.\n\nThe active egress gate calls this generated matcher and decision through the\ncomponent worker. The Python adapter preserves phrase order and supplies code\npoints and edge flags; Python string conversion, lowercasing, `isalnum`, JSON,\nthe adapter, generated-code loader and execution platform remain trusted. The\nproof does not establish that the phrase policy understands text or detects\nall unsafe responses. Dafny, its solver and compiler remain trusted.\n\n`negative/MissingLeftGuard.dfy` and `negative/MissingRightGuard.dfy` each remove\none executable boundary guard while retaining the specification. Both must fail\nverification. `metadata.json` binds the source, the exact mutants and generated\nPython hashes; the shared component checker re-verifies the proof and compares\nregenerated bytes when given the pinned Dafny toolchain.\n"},"language":"dafny","metadata_ref":"formal/components/egress_policy/metadata.json","module":"EgressPolicy","negative_controls":[{"changed_lines":[{"line":30,"mutated":"         true &&","original":"         (!left || i == 0 || !AsciiWord(t[i-1])) &&"}],"changed_lines_sha256":"f522cb7c2f92b50312babcd37f6891175892ad33805a197befffdaf79510f2e1","description":"Replaces 'if t[i..i + |p|] == p &&\\n         (!left || i == 0 || !AsciiWord(t[i-1])) &&\\n         (!right || i + |p| == |t| || !AsciiWord(t[i + |p|])) {' with 'if t[i..i + |p|] == p &&\\n         true &&\\n         (!right || i + |p| == |t| || !AsciiWord(t[i + |p|])) {'.","description_basis":"retained_mutation_recipe","fresh_result":{"status":"not_run_by_index"},"retained_result":{"basis":"recorded_metadata","errors":1,"verified_tasks":7},"source_ref":"formal/components/egress_policy/negative/MissingLeftGuard.dfy","source_sha256":"5d1e2f7a161a58c05766eadcc3eb2d0c7be9842caa24241e4d7a3f057c376757"},{"changed_lines":[{"line":31,"mutated":"         true {","original":"         (!right || i + |p| == |t| || !AsciiWord(t[i + |p|])) {"}],"changed_lines_sha256":"6cca96d4054bfb7625f8be808c505aa42973f2f0bb07f0f3ee36c7f45a05f854","description":"Replaces 'if t[i..i + |p|] == p &&\\n         (!left || i == 0 || !AsciiWord(t[i-1])) &&\\n         (!right || i + |p| == |t| || !AsciiWord(t[i + |p|])) {' with 'if t[i..i + |p|] == p &&\\n         (!left || i == 0 || !AsciiWord(t[i-1])) &&\\n         true {'.","description_basis":"retained_mutation_recipe","fresh_result":{"status":"not_run_by_index"},"retained_result":{"basis":"recorded_metadata","errors":1,"verified_tasks":7},"source_ref":"formal/components/egress_policy/negative/MissingRightGuard.dfy","source_sha256":"0b0794a